# 67. Cognitive Evaluation, Calibration and Self-Sufficiency

Artemis cognition must be evaluated as a system, not merely by measuring the
accuracy of one LLM or one Agent.

## 67.1 Cognitive-System Evaluation

Evaluation should distinguish, where meaningful:

- Evidence selection quality
- Exclusion quality
- Conflict detection quality
- Correlation handling quality
- Missing-evidence handling
- Abstention quality
- Scenario usefulness
- Decision calibration
- Directional usefulness
- Risk-flag recall
- Explanation faithfulness
- Decision stability under irrelevant input changes
- Robustness to one provider/model outage
- Robustness to stale or malformed evidence
- Latency
- Cost

## 67.2 Component vs System Performance

TitanGold must distinguish:

- Agent performance
- Advisor/model performance
- Router performance
- Memory retrieval performance
- Cognitive Kernel performance
- Artemis synthesis performance
- Control-chain performance
- Execution performance

A high-performing advisor does not prove that Artemis synthesis is good.

A good Artemis analytical decision does not prove execution quality.

## 67.3 Ablation and Dependency Measurement

Where practical, self-sufficiency claims should be supported by controlled
comparisons such as:

- Internal evidence only
- Internal evidence plus memory
- Internal evidence plus one advisor
- Internal evidence plus Council
- Local model versus external model
- With and without a specific Agent family

The purpose is to measure which capability materially improves the approved
workflow.

Do not use ablation results to bypass safety controls.

## 67.4 Self-Sufficiency Meaning

Artemis becomes more self-sufficient when the approved workflow remains within
quality, calibration, safety, provenance, latency and cost thresholds with less
routine dependency on external AI.

Self-sufficiency does not require zero external-AI usage.

External specialists may remain valuable for:

- Rare expertise
- Challenge
- Benchmarking
- Independent verification
- Incident analysis
- Model-diversity checks

## 67.5 No Automatic Cognitive Promotion

A model, routing policy, prompt policy, memory strategy or synthesis policy must
not be promoted to production merely because it appears better in one sample or
one backtest.

Promotion requires the applicable TitanGold lifecycle:

Offline validation
→ controlled evaluation
→ Shadow where applicable
→ Paper where applicable
→ Human QA
→ explicit production promotion

Execution maturity remains governed by Section 53.

